+version is part of the version gate tuple. All normalisation happens here; the
+raw memo is never changed (`NormalisedMemo.raw_memo`).
+
+**API** (`autobook.pipeline.normaliser`): `load(user_dir=None)` returns a
+`Normaliser`; `Normaliser.normalise(raw_memo, source_account)` returns a
+`NormalisedMemo` (`raw_memo`, `token`, `profile`, `version`). Every bad profile,
+pattern, mapping or account path raises `NormaliserError` (a `ValueError`) naming
+the file; nothing falls back silently.
+
+**Profile format.** A profile is a TOML file `<name>.toml`: an ordered list of
+`[[rules]]`, each with exactly one key, `pattern`, a Python `re` expression
+(literal TOML strings keep backslashes). Patterns run in file order on the
+upper-cased memo, so they are written in upper case, and every match is replaced
+by a space. Then whitespace runs collapse to one space and both ends are
+stripped; the result is the token, which may be empty. Any other key, a
+non-string pattern or a pattern that does not compile is an error.
+
+**Package profiles** live in `src/autobook/pipeline/profiles/`: `default` (card
+and reference fragments, dates, standalone digit runs, `SAGT DANKE`) and `sepa`
+(`default`, plus the `EREF+`, `MREF+`, `CRED+` and `ABWA+` tags with their values
+up to the next SEPA tag, and the `SVWZ+` tag alone, keeping the purpose text). A
+tag is found even with no space before it, as some exports join the fields.
+
+**User directory and override.** `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autobook/normaliser/` (see
+section 8.8). A `<name>.toml` there replaces the package profile of the same name
+entirely, with no merge; a new name adds a profile. Hidden files are ignored. A
+missing directory means package profiles only; one that exists but cannot be read
+is an error. `accounts.toml` maps source accounts to profiles:
+
+```toml
+[[accounts]]
+path = ["Aktiva", "Girokonto"]   # the account path as a list, never a joined string
+profile = "sepa"
+```
+
+Each entry has exactly `path` and `profile`; an unknown profile or an account
+mapped twice is an error. An account with no entry uses `default`.
+
+**Version.** `Normaliser.version` is `"<NORMALISER_VERSION>-<12 hex digits>"`:
+the code's algorithm version, and a SHA-256 digest of every effective profile
+(name and rules, in order) and the account mapping, sorted by profile name and
+account path. No file path, file name or timestamp enters the digest, so the same
+files give the same version from any directory, and one changed rule or mapping
+line gives a different one. This string, not the integer alone, is what is
+recorded with every vector and in the version tuple, and what
+`proposals.normaliser_version` will hold.
 
